# Jing's "Trajectory" arm on the nature CNN instead of DINO (2026-09-24, Joana).
#
# Why: chunk5 (DINO) is the only DINO arm that improves at all, and both nature-CNN
# arms are the only ones learning to avoid crashes while getting FASTER rather than
# slower. This is the matched pair that separates "chunking helps" from "the CNN
# helps" -- identical to trajectory_chunk5.env except the encoder.
#
# No box memory, matching trajectory_chunk5 exactly. Note the consequence: without
# BOXMEM the near-field collision box often fails to project, so the reward falls
# back to the far box and close-range contacts go unregistered. That is a property
# of the comparison, not a bug, but it means crash numbers for BOTH chunk arms are
# far-box numbers.
ENCODER=nature
IMGFIX=0
CHUNK=5
GPUS=4
